# Environment variables. Names only — this file never carries a value.
# Copy to .env for local work. .env is git-ignored; this file is not.
#
# =============================================================================
# NO SECRET MAY TAKE A PUBLIC_ PREFIX.
#
# SvelteKit inlines every PUBLIC_-prefixed variable into the client bundle at
# build time. Anything behind that prefix is published to every browser that
# loads the app, permanently, and cannot be un-published by rotating the
# deployment. The two blocks below are separated for that reason and must stay
# separated. A secret that appears in the second block is a breach, not a typo.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-only. Never prefixed PUBLIC_. Never imported into a .svelte file.
# Read through $env/static/private or $env/dynamic/private only.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Supabase — the project for this deploy context. production -> prod, every
# other context -> dev. The mapping is committed in netlify.toml.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET was listed here until Story 9.6 and is gone because NO
# CODE READS IT. The app never verifies a JWT itself: `@supabase/ssr` and
# supabase-js handle tokens against Supabase's own endpoints, and AD-15 resolves
# identity server-side from the `managers` table rather than from any claim. A
# contract file that names a variable nothing consumes sends the next operator
# hunting for a value that changes nothing.

# The direct/pooled Postgres connection `shell/db.ts` uses (AD-6). Distinct
# from SUPABASE_URL, which is the PostgREST endpoint every other server read
# goes through — this one holds `BEGIN ... pg_advisory_xact_lock ... COMMIT`
# open across a transaction, which PostgREST cannot do.
SUPABASE_DB_URL=

# Discord OAuth2 application — identity (AD-15). Discord is the only identity
# provider; there is no self-service registration and no email field anywhere.
#
# LOCAL ONLY, and not read by the app at all. The app does not hand-roll the
# OAuth flow — `server/supabase.ts` calls `signInWithOAuth({ provider:
# 'discord' })`, so Supabase owns the handshake. These two are consumed by
# `supabase config push` through the `env()` references in
# `supabase/config.toml`, which is where the provider is actually configured.
#
# Do NOT set them in Netlify: nothing there would read them.
#
# DISCORD_REDIRECT_URI was listed here and is gone (Story 9.6). It was read by
# nothing and actively misleading: Discord's redirect URI points at SUPABASE's
# callback (`https://<ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback`), never at this app,
# and it is registered in the Discord developer portal rather than set here.
DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=
DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Discord incoming webhook — notifications (AD-18). Write-only, 30 req/min.
#
# An EDGE FUNCTION SECRET, not a Netlify variable: the only reader is
# `supabase/functions/tick/`. Set it with `npx supabase secrets set`.
#
# DISCORD_GUILD_ID was listed here and is gone (Story 9.6) — read by nothing.
DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=

# The Commissioner sign-in that does not depend on Discord. Unadvertised but
# reachable, because Discord carries both authentication and notification and a
# Discord outage must not lock the referee out of the pause control.
COMMISSIONER_RECOVERY_SECRET=

# Shared secret the Supabase Cron tick presents when invoking the Edge Function.
#
# An EDGE FUNCTION SECRET, not a Netlify variable — the only reader is
# `supabase/functions/tick/auth.ts`. It is ALSO needed as a Vault secret named
# `tick_invocation_secret`, which the cron job reads by name so that no secret
# is ever a literal in a migration.
TICK_INVOCATION_SECRET=

# The app's own absolute origin — https://bbsl.example, scheme and host, no
# trailing slash and no path. The tick has no incoming request to take an origin
# from, and `core/auction-link.ts` answers a path and deliberately no host, so a
# Discord mention joins this onto the path to link a Manager straight at the
# Auction. Unset costs the link and never the notification.
#
# Server-only, and NEVER PUBLIC_-prefixed: it is not a secret, but no browser
# needs it — a browser already knows its own origin — and the prefix would inline
# a deployment's host into the client bundle for no reader.
#
# An EDGE FUNCTION SECRET, not a Netlify variable (Story 9.6): the only reader
# is `supabase/functions/tick/`, which is exactly what the paragraph above
# describes — the tick has no incoming request to take an origin from. Nothing
# in the SvelteKit app reads it, because a request there already carries one.
APP_ORIGIN=

# The Fantrax roster read — the divergence detector (Story 7.9, FR-42).
#
# Server-only, all five, and NONE may ever take a PUBLIC_ prefix: the league id
# identifies a private league, the invocation secret is a credential, and a
# browser has no use for any of them.
#
# FANTRAX_BASE_URL is the origin plus the API prefix and NO trailing path —
# https://www.fantrax.com/fxea/general. The endpoint's own path, its query
# parameter names and every field it returns live in
# src/lib/adapters/fantrax/roster-api.ts and nowhere else (AD-24); this variable
# exists so a move of the host is a variable change rather than a code change.
FANTRAX_BASE_URL=

# The Fantrax league to read. Getting this wrong does not fail: it succeeds and
# returns SOMEBODY ELSE'S rosters, which is precisely what the plausibility
# guard exists to refuse before anything is proposed from it.
FANTRAX_LEAGUE_ID=

# The scoring period to read rosters as of. Getting this wrong is the same class
# of fault as the league id — a plausible answer about the wrong thing.
FANTRAX_PERIOD=

# Shared secret /api/fantrax-read demands, presented as
# x-fantrax-read-invocation-secret. Deliberately NOT TICK_INVOCATION_SECRET: two
# jobs sharing one secret cannot be revoked separately, and this one reaches a
# third party while the tick reaches the auction itself.
#
# It is ALSO needed as a Vault secret named `fantrax_read_invocation_secret`,
# beside `fantrax_read_function_url`, which the scheduled cron job reads by name so
# that no secret is ever a literal in a migration.
FANTRAX_READ_INVOCATION_SECRET=

# OPTIONAL. The share of the League one comparison may touch before the
# plausibility guard trips — FR-42's "fraction tunable without a code change".
# A decimal strictly between 0 and 1; unset uses core/constants.ts's
# DIVERGENCE_VOLUME_FRACTION, a quarter. A value outside that range is IGNORED
# and logged rather than obeyed: a typo'd `25` would disarm the guard entirely,
# which is the one outcome a misconfiguration here must not be able to produce.
DIVERGENCE_VOLUME_FRACTION=

# Which Supabase project this deploy points at: "prod" or "dev". Set per context
# in netlify.toml; asserted by scripts/check-pins.js.
SUPABASE_ENVIRONMENT=
APP_ENV=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client-inlined. PUBLIC_ prefix. Assume every value here is world-readable.
# Nothing that grants a write may appear below this line.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The browser's Supabase connection, used only for read-only Realtime
# subscriptions. The anon role holds no write privilege on any table and every
# table carries an explicit row-level policy.
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
